- `## Review Phase Detail`
- `round acceptance table and per-round ASCII Gantt charts` (or equivalent)
- `Partial top-level bullets alone` / `contract violation`
**SKILL bash-fence absence check** (existing Python block style; extend the existing heredoc in the same function):
- Parse `skills/design/SKILL.md`.
- Extract all ` ```bash ` fenced bodies.
- Fail if any bash fence contains `LARCH_FINAL_SUMMARY_BEGIN`.
- Fail if any bash fence contains `LARCH_FINAL_SUMMARY_END`.
**Forbid pins** in final-summary emit contexts (targeted grep on `SKILL_MD` within the same function), for example:
- `same Read/\`cat\` mechanism`
- `from completed \`design-step5c.sh\` stdout` must not appear inside the `### Final summary block` post-notification paragraph (Step 5c abort/item-5 sites may still name `design-step5c.sh` as their fence)
- `After Step 5c \`design-publish.sh\` returns` must not appear in the `### Final summary block` post-notification paragraph (~349)
Keep existing **wrapper** marker assertions at lines 652–655 unchanged. Wrappers should still emit markers.
### UPDATED: scripts/test-implement-structure.sh
Add matching checks for `skills/implement/SKILL.md`:
- Parse all ` ```bash ` fenced bodies; fail on `LARCH_FINAL_SUMMARY_BEGIN` / `LARCH_FINAL_SUMMARY_END` inside bash fences.
**Positive prose pins:**
- no Bash/Python/tool invocation may print `summary-final.md` for user-visible delivery
- orchestrator must emit the body directly as chat markdown after `Read`
- `## Review Phase Detail` in mandatory full-body language (or equivalent)
- explicit retirement of `--print-stdout` as authorized body source (e.g. forbid pin on `write-final-report.sh --print-stdout` as the structured-block delivery anchor in NEVER #17 or Step 17 cost-line paragraph)
**Forbid pins** for retired allowed patterns:
- `via Bash \`cat\` whose output is then re-emitted`
- `write-final-report.sh --print-stdout` as the sole/canonical body-delivery anchor in NEVER #17 opening sentence (wrapper may still use the flag; SKILL prose must not authorize stdout delivery)
Do not move this harness (`scripts/test-implement-structure.sh`, backed by `make test-implement-structure`).
## Edge cases
- Markers may still appear in normal prose. That is allowed.
- Markers must still appear in wrapper scripts. That is required.
- The bash-fence test rejects markers only inside ` ```bash ` fences in `SKILL.md`.
- The fallback file path may be non-empty when markers are absent. The prompt must still emit the fallback body as chat text, not tool stdout.
- `REPORT_GATE_SIDECARS_FILE` is a machine KV in wrapper output: orchestrator may **read** it from the Read result in context, but must **not** Bash/Python-extract or Bash/Python-print the sidecar body.
- Step 18b may refresh `summary-final.md` after Step 17. Keep the existing `EMIT_BODY=true` gate.
- The anti-halt paragraph is long and dense. Add the delivery-channel prohibition without weakening "do not end the turn on Bash result" or "no free-form recap."
- **`--print-stdout` vs Read:** `step-17.sh` may continue passing `--print-stdout` to `write-final-report.sh`; only SKILL prose changes. Orchestrators must load body from `summary-final.md` via Read, not from Bash stdout (FINDING_1).
- Unrelated stdout/KV parsing (Step 0 bootstrap, publish `_publish_rc`, OOS filing env capture) is unchanged.
## Failure modes
- If the implementer uses `grep -R` over all logs, old run logs may create noisy hits. Scope tests to the live skill files.
- If the new text says "tool invocation" without carving out `Read`, it may sound like `Read` is banned. Word it as "do not use a tool invocation to **print** the body; use `Read` only to bring text into context."
- If `.step17-emitted` wording changes too much, existing sentinel semantics may become unclear. Preserve the sentinel contract.
- If stdout wording survives at one emit site (863, 867, 349, 882–884, anti-halt ~29), orchestrators may still treat Bash/Python tool output as authorized delivery and omit `## Review Phase Detail`.
- If `### Final summary block` (~349) still opens with Step 5c / `_publish_rc`, cancellation-path orchestrators may Read the wrong completed task (FINDING_2).
- If NEVER #17 or Step 17 (~818) still anchor on `--print-stdout`, orchestrators may skip full verbatim chat emission including `## Review Phase Detail` (FINDING_1).
- If legacy `contains` pins at `test-design-structure.sh` lines 656–657 are left alongside the new pins, `make test-design-structure` will fail after correct SKILL edits even though the feature is implemented.
## Testing strategy
Run focused structure tests:
- `make test-design-structure`
- `make test-implement-structure`
Run the repo-relevant check selector after edits:
- `bash scripts/relevant-checks.sh`
Optional negative checks:
- Temporarily place `LARCH_FINAL_SUMMARY_BEGIN` inside a `bash` fence in `skills/design/SKILL.md`; `make test-design-structure` should fail.
- Temporarily place `LARCH_FINAL_SUMMARY_BEGIN` inside a `bash` fence in `skills/implement/SKILL.md`; `make test-implement-structure` should fail.
- Temporarily remove `## Review Phase Detail` from one mandatory-body enumeration in `skills/design/SKILL.md`; `make test-design-structure` should fail on the new positive prose pin.
- Temporarily restore `After Step 5c \`design-publish.sh\` returns` inside the `### Final summary block` post-notification paragraph (~349); `make test-design-structure` should fail on the new forbid pin.
- Temporarily restore the legacy line-656 `contains` pin while SKILL prose uses Read-to-orchestrator-text only; `make test-design-structure` should fail (confirms retire/replace, not additive drift).
- Temporarily restore `write-final-report.sh --print-stdout` as the NEVER #17 body-delivery anchor in `skills/implement/SKILL.md`; `make test-implement-structure` should fail on the new forbid pin.
